        "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-4\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
